  "title": "Xuanzang's journey to India",
  "summary": "In 629 the Chinese Buddhist monk Xuanzang left Chang'an for India despite an imperial ban on western travel. He passed through Turfan, where the king tried to keep him, and Samarkand, and is dated at Bamiyan in 632 and at Nalanda in 637. He returned to Chang'an in 645, welcomed in triumph, and composed his account of the western regions in 646.",
