  "reviewer_note": "Least sure: intermediate dates. Turfan and Samarkand appear on opened pages without years, so they are not waypoints. 632 (Bamiyan) and 637 (Nalanda) come from one non-scholarly timeline and conflict with other accounts (Encyclopedia.com: arrival in India 633). Only the 629 start and 645 return are confirmed by two reference sources. Bamiyan pin is the town, not the Buddha niches.",
